    "result_text": "Done. The suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## What I changed\n\nTwo files, both minimal:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipNumber` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto`, right alongside the existing `displayName` expression:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"membershipNumber\", expression = \"java(owner.getCustomerCode() == null || owner.getRegistrationDate() == null ? null : owner.getCustomerCode() + \\\"-M\\\" + String.format(\\\"%02d\\\", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100))\")\n   ```\n   This produces `<customerCode>-M<YY>` (e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`), deriving `YY` from the last two digits of the registration-date year.\n\n## Why this shape (low structural impact)\n\nI derived the value at mapping time rather than storing it:\n\n- **No new DB column** \u2014 avoids editing `schema.sql` and every positional `INSERT` in `data.sql`.\n- **No new pipeline step / YAML** and **no changes to the large `Owner` entity class** (whose high `WMC_other` would dominate the cost formula).\n- Only the small `OwnerMapper` interface method is modified (tiny surrounding complexity) plus the schema \u2014 **2 files touched**.\n- The null-guard keeps it safe for seed owners (which have `NULL` customer code / registration date), matching the test's \"derived from the owner's own fields, so seed-independent\" contract.",
